  "version_ordering_comment": "Ordering-level binding between Compendium.Semver.compare/2 (Elixir) and ref.CompareVersions (Go). The regex pin covers the grammar and `cases` covers parse verdicts; neither covered ORDERING, and the two sides once disagreed on every mixed pair (Go byte-compared when either side failed the grammar; the server ranks the parsable side higher and byte-compares only when both fail). expect is gt/lt/eq for a-versus-b.",
  "version_ordering": [
    { "a": "1.0.0", "b": "0.9.9", "expect": "gt" },
    { "a": "0.9.9", "b": "1.0.0", "expect": "lt" },
    { "a": "1.0.0", "b": "1.0.0", "expect": "eq" },
    { "a": "1.0.0", "b": "1.0.0-rc.1", "expect": "gt" },
    { "a": "1.0.0-rc.1", "b": "1.0.0", "expect": "lt" },
    { "a": "1.0.0-alpha", "b": "1.0.0-1", "expect": "gt" },
    { "a": "1.0.0+build.1", "b": "1.0.0+build.2", "expect": "eq" },
    { "a": "1.0.0", "b": "not-semver", "expect": "gt" },
    { "a": "not-semver", "b": "1.0.0", "expect": "lt" },
    { "a": "abc", "b": "abd", "expect": "lt" },
    { "a": "abd", "b": "abc", "expect": "gt" },
    { "a": "garbage", "b": "garbage", "expect": "eq" }
  ],
  "tincture_urls_comment": "The tincture URL grammar Prima.TinctureUrl writes: a tincture's public path, /t/<athanor>/<publisher>/<name>, and a private version's served file, /_s/<credential>/<path inside the version>, under an asset credential that is opaque, URL-safe (base64url segments joined by dots), 16 to 1024 characters and never leads with a dot. parse is what a served-file path reads back as: the credential and the file's segments, or null when the path is refused. Prima's test reads these cases.",
